  <title>7.13.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01978</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.13.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>2e4a710f-5659-473b-b4e3-c840d5e804ee</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="10c18699-63a8-4727-aef9-554b952c18ad"><problem><para>
      <para>Choose the quadratic equation that represents each graph.</para>
      <para>
            <para><figure><media alt="&lt;p&gt;A curve in an x y plane, origin O. Horizontal axis, scale negative 6 to 5, by 1’s. Vertical axis, scale negative 4 to 4, by 1’s. A curve passes through the points negative 2 comma 2, 0 comma 0, and 2 comma 6.&lt;/p&gt;"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/7dc411bbf2270de91b8434022d10d52c2ef5b03d"/></media></figure></para>
          </para>
        </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(y=x^2+x\)</para><para>\(y=-x^2+2\)</para><para>\(y=x^2-x\)</para><para>\(y=x^2+3x\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(y=x^2+x\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is: \(y=x^2+x\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><!--BEGIN PRACTICE PROBLEM MULTIPLE CHOICE -->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="d5887686-b139-4874-86d2-d295948cb807"><problem><para>
      <para>Choose the quadratic equation written from the real solutions \(x=-4\) and \(x=-3\). </para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(y=x^2-7x+12\)</para><para>\(y=x^2+7x+12\)</para><para>\(y=x^2+7x-12\)</para><para>\(y=x^2-7x-12\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(y=x^2+7x+12\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(y=x^2+7x+12\).</para>
      <para>\(x=-4\) and \(x=-3\) means that \(x+4=0\) and \(x+3=0\). \(y=(x+4)(x+3) = x^2+3x+4x+12 = x^2+7x+12.\)
      </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><!--END PRACTICE PROBLEM MULTIPLE CHOICE --></section>
</content>
